\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O how blest the hour, Lord Jesus,
\par Where we can to Thee draw near,
\par Promises so sweet and precious
\par From Thy gracious lips to hear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Be with us this day to bless us,
\par That we may not hear in vain;
\par With the saving truths impress us,
\par Which the words of life contain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Open Thou our minds, and lead us
\par Safely on our heavenward way,
\par With the lamp of truth precede us,
\par That we may not go astray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Make us gentle, meek, and humble,
\par And yet bold in doing right:
\par Scatter darkness, lest we stumble;
\par Men walk safely in the light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, endue Thy word from heaven
\par With such light, and love, and power,
\par That in us its silent leaven
\par May work on from hour to hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 6. Give us grace to bear our witness,
\par To the truths we have embraced;
\par And let others both their sweetness
\par And their quickening virtue taste.
\par                                       Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

